				<r3d:description language="eng">All ADNI data are shared without embargo through the LONI Image and Data Archive (IDA), a secure research data repository. Interested scientists may obtain access to ADNI imaging, clinical, genomic, and biomarker data for the purposes of scientific investigation, teaching, or planning clinical research studies.
&quot;The Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI) unites researchers with study data as they work to define the progression of Alzheimer’s disease (AD). ADNI researchers collect, validate and utilize data, including MRI and PET images, genetics, cognitive tests, CSF and blood biomarkers as predictors of the disease. Study resources and data from the North American ADNI study are available through this website, including Alzheimer’s disease patients, mild cognitive impairment subjects, and elderly controls. &quot;</r3d:description>
